      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your 12 engineers traveling through Singapore, Vietnam, and Thailand, standard tourist visitor visas (not transit visas) are generally required for entry, as these countries rarely grant visa-on-arrival exemptions for engineering visas unless specifically pre-approved. Always verify if your flight layover in Vietnam requires you to collect bags and pass through immigration, as transit visas only apply to those remaining in the international transit zone without entering the country. To avoid detention or entry denial, ensure all border officers have a clear explanation of your itinerary, valid return tickets, and proof of accommodation before departure. Consulting with your assigned immigration lawyer or the specific visa sponsor handling your group is also crucial, as regulations can change frequently for technical visitors.",
