      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is unfortunate that bureaucratic unpredictability occurs, but being rude or confrontational during an inspection—especially with border guards or clerks—can lead to detention or deportation. Instead, prepare the engineers to remain calm, respectful, and willing to provide additional documentation on the spot before escalating to a higher-level officer or filing an official appeal. Practicing scenario-based role-play where they can memorize key phrases like \"I understand there may be more information needed; I am willing to provide it\" can help de-escalate tension without compromising their professional integrity. Ultimately, recording the interaction (if local laws permit) or having a legal representative present at key checkpoints often provides the necessary leverage to resolve these \"weird\" situations fairly.",
